{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2440","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2440","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2440\",\"parent_revision\":\"8e889281d900b1503db916d82cad53c3a20634cf\",\"root_revision\":\"b25329e6bd939c1fd0deca72c903201238b72b4ed496ece082e6c7b0c2d95803\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nDuring QG feature verification (P60d669b9/T2, issue #2279), fastmcp CLI tests of the backlog MCP server produced `Connection closed` errors due to path doubling.\\n\\n**Root cause:** When fastmcp spawns `uv run --script plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_backlog_server.py` using a relative path, uv resolves the path relative to the development-harness venv root (not the repo root), producing a doubled path: `.../plugins/development-harness/plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_backlog_server.py`. The script is not found and the server fails to start.\\n\\n**Also observed:** When using an absolute path to the server script, the spawned fastmcp subprocess does not inherit env vars (e.g. `BACKLOG_BACKEND`) set in the calling process. This means env-var-controlled routing (beads vs GitHub) cannot be tested via fastmcp CLI.\\n\\n**Impact:** Cannot use fastmcp CLI for discriminating integration tests of env-var-controlled backend routing. Currently worked around by direct Python import tests (which use the production in-process code path correctly). The path doubling affects only fastmcp CLI invocation \u2014 production MCP server operation via Claude Code plugin infrastructure is unaffected.\\n\\n**Required action:** Investigate how fastmcp resolves `--command` paths and whether `--env` flag or subprocess env propagation can be fixed to support proper integration testing.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **fix fastmcp cli path doubling when invoking run_backlog_server.py with relative path** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: QG feature verification P60d669b9/T2 non-blocking finding (2026-05-15)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-15\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-28)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS**\\n\\n**Functional intent** \u2014 AVAILABLE. The item clearly describes two distinct bugs: (1) path doubling when fastmcp CLI receives a relative path to `run_backlog_server.py`, and (2) env-var non-inheritance in the spawned subprocess. Both failure modes are observable and described with a root cause hypothesis.\\n\\n**Scope boundaries** \u2014 AVAILABLE. Production MCP operation via Claude Code plugin infrastructure is explicitly out of scope. In-scope: fastmcp CLI integration testing of env-var-controlled backend routing.\\n\\n**External interfaces** \u2014 PARTIAL. `fastmcp` CLI path resolution behavior is referenced but not verified against fastmcp source or docs. The `--env` flag existence for `fastmcp call` is unconfirmed (local search found `--env-file` for `fastmcp install` only, not for `fastmcp call`). DERIVABLE via `fastmcp call --help` or source inspection.\\n\\n**Constraints** \u2014 AVAILABLE. uv PEP 723 `--script` flag; repo root as working directory requirement.\\n\\n**Existing system context** \u2014 AVAILABLE. `run_backlog_server.py` uses `Path(__file__).resolve()` for all internal path construction. CLAUDE.md already mandates `$(pwd)/...` (absolute path) for fastmcp CLI invocations.\\n\\n**Verification expectations** \u2014 PARTIAL. No reproducible test command is captured in the item. Fix is verifiable by running fastmcp CLI against the server with both a relative path and an absolute path with `BACKLOG_BACKEND=memory` set.\\n\\n**Missing inputs:**\\n\\n- Whether `fastmcp call` CLI supports a `--env KEY=VALUE` flag (affects second fix approach)\\n- Exact fastmcp version constraint driving the behavior\\n- Whether path doubling is a fastmcp behavior or a uv `--script` behavior when resolving relative paths\\n\\n**Impact of incorrect assumption:** If `--env` is not supported on `fastmcp call`, the env-var propagation fix requires a different approach (wrapper script, `.env` file, or env-var prefix). Risk is medium \u2014 wrong approach choice adds rework.\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n1. From the repo root, run `uv run fastmcp list --command \\\"uv run --script plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_backlog_server.py\\\"` \u2014 observe `Connection closed` error.\\n2. Inspect error output or enable verbose logging to confirm path contains doubled `plugins/development-harness/plugins/development-harness/`.\\n3. Retry with absolute path: `uv run fastmcp list --command \\\"uv run --script $(pwd)/plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_backlog_server.py\\\"` \u2014 observe successful tool listing.\\n4. Run step 3 with `BACKLOG_BACKEND=memory` prefix \u2014 observe whether the spawned server picks up the env var (expected: it does NOT, confirming second bug).\\n\\nNote: Steps 1-2 produce `Connection closed`. Step 4 requires the env var test to be deterministic \u2014 verify by calling `backlog_list` with a `BACKLOG_BACKEND=memory` prefix and checking whether response comes from memory backend (no GitHub credentials required).\\n\\n### Output / Evidence\\n\\n- `Connection closed` error from `fastmcp list`/`fastmcp call` when using relative path.\\n- Doubled path visible in fastmcp error output or server startup log: `.../plugins/development-harness/plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_backlog_server.py`.\\n- When env var not inherited: `backlog_list` returns GitHub backend responses even when `BACKLOG_BACKEND=memory` is set in caller env.\\n- Source of original observation: QG feature verification P60d669b9/T2, issue #2279 (2026-05-15). Already worked around by using direct Python import tests.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n4/10 \u2014 P2 (could-have). Production MCP operation is unaffected. Current workaround (direct Python import tests) covers the env-var routing test cases. Only integration testing via fastmcp CLI is impaired. Low urgency but a clean fix removes a confusing limitation documented in CLAUDE.md.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: discriminating integration tests of env-var-controlled backend routing via fastmcp CLI.\\n- Bottleneck: developers cannot use `BACKLOG_BACKEND=memory fastmcp call` to run isolated integration tests without GitHub credentials; must use Python import tests instead.\\n- No impact on Claude Code production plugin operation.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Unlocks `BACKLOG_BACKEND=memory/sqlite fastmcp call` as a credential-free integration test path.\\n- Documents correct invocation pattern in CLAUDE.md, preventing recurrence.\\n- Enables future CI tests that exercise the full MCP server path without live GitHub credentials.\\n- Removes documented workaround caveat from CLAUDE.md.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\n1. `uv run fastmcp list --command \\\"uv run --script plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_backlog_server.py\\\"` succeeds from repo root \u2014 tool list returned, no `Connection closed` error.\\n2. `BACKLOG_BACKEND=memory uv run fastmcp call --command \\\"uv run --script $(pwd)/plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_backlog_server.py\\\" backlog_list '{}'` routes to memory backend \u2014 response contains no GitHub-dependent data.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\n- fastmcp CLI invocations in CLAUDE.md and all documentation always use absolute paths (via `$(pwd)/...`) \u2014 no relative paths.\\n- A reproducible test command (or pytest integration test) demonstrates both correct path resolution and env-var inheritance.\\n- If `fastmcp call` does not support `--env`, the documentation records the correct workaround (env var prefix on the outer command) and notes fastmcp does not forward env vars by default.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. Running `uv run fastmcp list --command \\\"uv run --script plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_backlog_server.py\\\"` from repo root exits 0 with a tool list, OR documentation explicitly states relative paths are unsupported and all documented invocations use `$(pwd)/...` absolute paths.\\n2. Running `BACKLOG_BACKEND=memory uv run fastmcp call --command \\\"uv run --script $(pwd)/plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_backlog_server.py\\\" backlog_list '{}'` returns a successful response from the memory backend (no GitHub credential required).\\n3. CLAUDE.md documents whether the path doubling is a fastmcp bug, a uv behavior, or a documented constraint \u2014 and the correct invocation form.\\n4. If `fastmcp call` supports `--env KEY=VALUE`, the CLAUDE.md backend testing section documents it. If not, it documents the env-var prefix pattern as the supported approach.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| File | plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_backlog_server.py |\\n| File | plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md (fastmcp validation instructions, lines 437-500) |\\n| File | plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backend_protocol.py (BACKLOG_BACKEND env var resolution, line 1046) |\\n| Skill | /fastmcp-creator:fastmcp-creator |\\n| Skill | /fastmcp-creator:fastmcp-client-cli |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md \u2014 existing `$(pwd)/...` invocation pattern and `BACKLOG_BACKEND=memory` backend testing guidance |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 standalone fix.\\n- Blocks: None directly. Unblocks cleaner integration test coverage for backend routing (future test work).\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- fastmcp CLI `--env` flag support on `fastmcp call` is unverified. Run `uv run fastmcp call --help` to confirm. This determines the implementation approach for the env-var propagation fix.\\n- Exact fastmcp version in use not confirmed \u2014 behavior may differ across versions. Check `uv run python -c \\\"import fastmcp; print(fastmcp.__version__)\\\"` before fixing.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 the path doubling fix is likely documentation only (update all relative-path invocations to use `$(pwd)/...`; this pattern already exists in CLAUDE.md). The env-var propagation issue requires one additional investigation step (verify `--env` flag support) then either documentation or a small wrapper. Total estimated effort: 1-2 hours.\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\nThis item aligns with the DH plugin's testing-against-fresh-source principle documented in CLAUDE.md: `fastmcp call` is the designated tool for testing `backlog_core/` changes before cache reload. Fixing path resolution and env-var propagation extends that testing capability to cover backend routing \u2014 a core behavioral axis of the server. Fixing the documented limitation also removes a source of confusion for contributors following CLAUDE.md instructions.\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Defect** \u2014 two reproducible bugs in the fastmcp CLI integration path:\\n1. Path doubling: fastmcp CLI resolves relative script paths relative to the development-harness venv root instead of the repo root CWD.\\n2. Env-var non-inheritance: spawned fastmcp subprocess does not inherit env vars set in the calling process.\\n\\nNeither affects production (Claude Code plugin infrastructure uses a different code path). Both affect integration testing of env-var-controlled backend routing.\\n\",\"digest\":\"3ec32c39bb44629c4d13245f9cfce5151f865c2d3ff166604961b4013f2a121e\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPnLr7w\"}"}